    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/sthubbar/goldbach-lean/tree/main/entries/hardylittlewood1923",
        "note": "The Hardy-Littlewood 1923 entry of this repository proves Theorem A of Partitio Numerorum III on the paper's Hypothesis R at level Theta, the same kind of zero-free half plane hypothesis for all Dirichlet L-functions, for sums of r >= 3 primes and only for 47/64 <= Theta < 3/4. It has no statement about the binary exceptional set E of X.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-10-21-000005",
        "note": "The Heath-Brown 1985 entry of this repository proves, with no hypothesis, that E of X is O of X divided by any power of log X, the theorem of van der Corput, Chudakov and Estermann, Theorem 4.3 of the survey.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-11-16-000013",
        "note": "The Estermann 1938 entry of this repository proves that the exceptional set has density zero, without a zero hypothesis.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-11-16-000024",
        "note": "The Pintz 2018 entry of this repository proves the weighted density and optimisation steps of Pintz's method for E of X below X to the power 0.72; the zero density inputs and the bound itself are not proved there.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-11-19-000032",
        "note": "The Brüdern and Perelli 1998 entry of this repository proves their Theorem 2 on exponential sums, from Karacuba's estimate taken as a hypothesis; it does not bound E of X.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-11-15-000007",
        "note": "Primes in arithmetic progressions with power-saving error from zero-free half-planes of Dirichlet L-functions, by Richard Morley-Smith, proves the bound for psi of x, q and a from a zero-free half plane Re s > Theta. Independent work; no code from it is used here. A search of the web and of the Palomar registry listing on 2026-11-22 found no earlier Lean formalization of a conditional bound for the binary Goldbach exceptional set.",
        "relationship": "other"
      }
    ],
